# Files whose bytes are hashed or compared (a level file's digest is part of a replay's checks, and a
# replay, a baked navmesh and a save must read the same on every OS) are checked out with LF on Windows
# too, whatever core.autocrlf says. Found by cross.yml: ruin.gltf came out with CRLF and three reference
# replays that place a level diverged on windows-latest ("replay check level differs").
*.gltf text eol=lf
*.ron text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.scenario text eol=lf
*.ftl text eol=lf
*.wesl text eol=lf
*.glb binary
*.save binary
*.wav binary
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
